1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:07,584
Quiet Margin. Trade Bitcoin perps on NEAR testnet. Watch what
the trader sees, what anyone can see, and what happens when

2
00:00:07,584 --> 00:00:09,056
the trader goes offline.

3
00:00:11,743 --> 00:00:18,741
Connect the public NEAR wallet, then sign a message to unlock
the private trading wallet. This signature moves no funds.

4
00:00:21,618 --> 00:00:29,269
Claim one hundred mock U S D C to the public wallet. Deposit
one hundred into the shielded pool and approve the public

5
00:00:29,269 --> 00:00:29,853
transfer.

6
00:00:30,327 --> 00:00:37,470
The testnet publisher relays a real Bitcoin price from
Binance. This receipt shows the on chain mark that settles the

7
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:37,836
trade.

8
00:00:38,327 --> 00:00:47,298
Open a point zero zero one Bitcoin short with thirty mock U S
D C of isolated margin. The browser proves it. Seventy stays

9
00:00:47,298 --> 00:00:48,033
available.

10
00:00:48,493 --> 00:00:56,129
On the left, the trader sees side, size, and margin. On the
right, a public observer sees the private signer, entry mark,

11
00:00:56,129 --> 00:01:03,827
commitments, and proof. The exact trade terms are absent from
the open arguments. Designated keepers can read them. Public

12
00:01:03,827 --> 00:01:06,477
funding and timing can help link activity.

13
00:01:06,952 --> 00:01:10,194
The block explorer shows where NEAR included this private
open.

14
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:17,543
Close against the live settlement mark. At the same mark, the
thirty returns to the shielded balance. The public wallet

15
00:01:17,543 --> 00:01:18,873
balance stays the same.

16
00:01:19,327 --> 00:01:26,482
The close posts a note commitment and public maker credit.
Settlement accounting and price movement can sometimes reveal

17
00:01:26,482 --> 00:01:31,252
position size or direction. The collateral stays in a note the
trader can spend.

18
00:01:31,743 --> 00:01:39,181
Withdraw ten to the connected public NEAR address. Ninety
stays shielded. The token transfer exposes the amount and

19
00:01:39,181 --> 00:01:39,957
destination.

20
00:01:44,743 --> 00:01:52,787
Same contract code, separate testnet pool. We control the mark
here so we can reproduce liquidation on demand. Trader A opens

21
00:01:52,787 --> 00:01:56,647
a long. Trader B opens a short. Both trading sessions close.

22
00:02:00,452 --> 00:02:07,744
At sixty eight thousand eight hundred, NEAR rejects Keeper B’s
long liquidation proof. The proof was built for an adverse

23
00:02:07,744 --> 00:02:11,481
price. The actual mark is healthy, so the position stays open.

24
00:02:15,452 --> 00:02:23,584
The controlled mark drops to forty thousand. Keeper B proves
the long is below maintenance and NEAR accepts it. One point

25
00:02:23,584 --> 00:02:25,734
two mock U S D C stays shielded.

26
00:02:26,202 --> 00:02:33,942
The short also shows a healthy rejection and an accepted
Keeper B liquidation after the controlled mark rises to ninety

27
00:02:33,942 --> 00:02:36,868
six thousand. Two point eight stays shielded.
